From 28bd7caaaf932bfaf112ef291aebbc1b32823f98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Can H. Tartanoglu" <gpg@rotas.mozmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Apr 2026 17:02:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: zero-cost rescue with user-chosen matching mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a restore token resolves to restore_data but the target window is
not yet running, the backend now checks restore_policy for the
source_unavailable reason:

  action 0 (prompt): show picker dialog as before
  action 1 (skip):   register rescue hook — wait up to 30s for
                      the window to appear; if session closed, cancel
  action 2 (error):  same as skip, but return restore_failure on
                      session close

The rescue mechanism uses a zero-cost hook system: PendingRescue structs
are stored in a Vec and checked inside the existing Wayland toplevel
event handler. No tokio tasks, no futures parked, no polling. Dead
rescues (session closed) are purged via oneshot::Sender::is_closed().

New: user-chosen rescue mode per window, selected in the picker dialog:

  Exact (0): only match by compositor identifier (same window instance)
  App   (1): match by app_id — grab any window from the same app
  Title (2): match by app_id + window title

The matching uses a tiered fallback: exact identifier first, then the
user-chosen mode. Empty app_id guards prevent false positives for
XWayland windows without WM_CLASS.

Restore data bumped from version 1 to 2 to store app_ids, titles, and
rescue_modes. V1 data deserializes with padded vecs (exact-only matching).

Also adds source_label and restore_policy to SelectSourcesOptions,
and bumps the backend interface version from 4 to 6.

Improvements over initial RFC draft:
- source_label sanitized: control chars stripped, 256-byte truncation
- V1/V2 parallel vec lengths validated at deserialization
- Rescue check-and-register is atomic (no TOCTOU race)
- Pending rescues capped at 64 (prevents resource exhaustion)
- Rescue timeout: 30 seconds (prevents indefinite hangs)
- Bounds-safe indexing for rescue mode updates in dialog
